-- title:
--   Smooth neighbourhood at a good point of the descended model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with value of the geometric $j$-generator in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from the geometric full-level-$M'$ field to that residual function field (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a compatible place map, and the usual compatibilities), assumed coefficientwise: every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Fix $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, an index $\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, and families of valuation subrings $O_{\mathrm{Ig}} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \to$ valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}} : W \to$ valuation subrings thereof, subject to: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of those $f$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f\,y = x$; each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \infty = \ell$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective and the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$-pullbacks permute its values; $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, is fixed by all these pullbacks, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for all $a \in A$, and receives from $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the stated reduction compatibility (elements regular wherever $j$ is and with residue in the valuation ring of $s$ land in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with the prescribed congruence to elements of $A$ modulo the maximal ideal). On the descent side, let $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a subfield with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$, and let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, inducing a surjection onto $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$. Let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, assume the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j_q$ lies in $F_0$ and is nonzero, and let $F_0$ carry an $A_0$-algebra structure whose structure map is $\iota$ followed by $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Finally let $x$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$ (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A_0[\hat\jmath]$ and $A_0[\hat\jmath^{-1}]$ in $F_0$) such that: $x$ maps to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$; $x$ is closed, in the sense that any point to which $x$ specialises equals $x$; for every point $y$ of either chart lying over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ lies in the prime of $y$; and for every point $y$ of the $\hat\jmath$-finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(\hat\jmath)$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$. Then there is an open subscheme $U$ of the two-chart model containing $x$ such that the inclusion of $U$ followed by the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ is smooth.
--
--   This is the "good point has a smooth neighbourhood" statement for the two-chart integral model, transported from the finite-layer setting to the descended data $(A_0, F_0, \hat\jmath)$ over a henselian discrete valuation ring: a closed point of the special fibre lying on the $\infty$-Igusa (Gauss) branch and ordinary in the sense that no chart point over it has supersingular $\hat\jmath$-value admits a neighbourhood smooth over the base. It feeds the dichotomy statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent) in the construction of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve.
